// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/events_booking.t27 -- the event booking machine: seats, the waitlist, and the
; day an event belongs to.
; One boundary, drawn twice. Sideways: between a seat that is HELD and a place in a line that
; holds nothing, and the arithmetic that decides which door a customer walks through. Downward:
; between an instant stored in UTC and the DATE a customer reads off a calendar, which is the
; only collision rule this surface actually has. This file owns capacity and the exact-capacity
; case, the three booking states, the waitlist's admission and promotion rules, the cancel-refund
; shape, and the month arithmetic's boundary cases. It owns no person, no money vocabulary, no
; clock and no proof of identity: who a request is belongs to turbobaby/request-identity, the wall
; clock and the offset belong to turbobaby/market, what an unpublished locale renders belongs to
; turbobaby/locale-policy, the distinction between a hidden row and a live surface belongs to
; turbobaby/legacy-retirement, a queued outbound message belongs to turbobaby/notification-queue,
; and what a sold-out event is WORTH to the promo sweeper belongs to turbobaby/promo-broadcast, and
; whether an attempt is admitted inside a window belongs to turbobaby/rate-limit. Seven edges,
; named here and below by ID and by declaration name, and not one of them restated. (The seven were
; spelled as FILE NAMES in this paragraph until 2026-09-21; a file name is not a contract's name,
; and the edge block below always used the IDs. Aligned so both halves of the file say the same.)
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). The number that forces this file is a ZERO, and it is a zero over
; src/, not over specs/. src/api/events.rs is 2496 lines -- it was 1959 when this file was written
; earlier the same day and 2290 after the delete refusal and the waitlist scan; the 206 lines since
; are the delete's escape hatch, its tests and the comments that say why. Its routes() at :29-53
; declares 11 HTTP
; paths carrying 14 method bindings into 14 handlers, and src/api/mod.rs:90 merges them into the
; public router unconditionally; src/ui/routes.rs:39-42 routes two screens onto them. Against all
; of that, migration 085 retired exactly NONE: its only touch on this surface is one visibility
; UPDATE at migrations/085_unpublish_woody_catalog.sql:25, which carries `WHERE is_public = TRUE`
; and therefore cannot reach a row that does not exist yet. migrations/043_events_booking.sql:17
; gives the column NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE and the create handler defaults the same way at
; src/api/events.rs:211. So the first TurboBaby event the owner inserts is public the instant it
; lands, on a machine whose capacity rule, waitlist rule and promotion rule had no contract.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24, and the paragraph above is kept as the reading it was. Two of its sentences
; stopped being true that day, one of them was never quite true, and the numbers are pinned below
; under their own names with the old values kept beside them. "Routes two screens onto them" was
; short by one: src/ui/routes.rs declared THREE client paths onto this surface -- /events and
; /events/:id at :39-42, and /my-bookings at :43-44, whose handler mounted this module's
; MyBookingsScreen -- and since the owner's ruling of 2026-09-24 (rental only, Phuket only;
; turbobaby/legacy-retirement records it) all three render the live catalog instead, as /sets does.
; And "public the instant it lands" is over: the admin API now stores an event's flag ANDed with
; EVENTS_PUBLISHABLE, which is false, so no event it creates or edits is public; every customer
; read below filters on that flag; and migrations/088_unpublish_events.sql hides, in 085's shape,
; any row still public when it runs. The HTTP router did not move -- it is still merged, and
; neither hide became a retirement of it.
; --
; THE SHARPEST SINGLE MEASUREMENT is the pair of comparisons that decide which door opens.
; src/api/events.rs:626 refuses a booking on `taken + seats > cap`; src/api/events.rs:1359 refuses
; a waitlist join on `taken < cap`. Equality belongs to the booking side: at taken + seats == cap
; the seat is SOLD, not refused. The two predicates are exact complements for a one-seat booking,
; so for any cap of one or more there is never a state where both doors are open and never a state
; where both are shut -- except cap == 0, where both ARE shut, and that state is reachable because
; migrations/043_events_booking.sql:20 permits max_seats = 0 and src/api/events.rs:196-200 admits
; it. That exception is declared below rather than smoothed over.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Five corrections, each measured 2026-09-21.
;   1. "About 8 routes" undercounts. src/api/events.rs:29-53 has 11 `.route(` paths and 14 method
;      bindings (:42 binds two, :43-46 binds three), resolving to 14 distinct handlers. The eight
;      in the survey is the count turbobaby/legacy-retirement measured for LEGACY SCREEN routes and
;      declares in LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTE_COUNT -- re-opened 2026-09-21 and still 8 -- a different
;      surface; the events screens are two of them, at src/ui/routes.rs:39-42.
;   2. "An attendee reachout is a queue row" is refuted at both of the tree's two reachouts.
;      send_event_reminders sends directly at src/api/events.rs:2130 and send_event_bookings sends
;      directly at :2026. A grep for `notification` over src/api/events.rs returns 0, and
;      src/db/notifications.rs declared exactly three enqueue functions (:16, :38, :52), all three
;      referral; since 2026-09-26 (R3) it declares one (:16), and the other two are dated comments
;      where they stood. The consequence is not cosmetic: the queue retries three times
;      (src/notification_queue.rs:21, was :20) and a direct send has one attempt and a `continue`
;      (src/api/events.rs:2134-2142). The edge to notification-queue is still taken below, as the
;      owner of the shape these two reachouts do NOT use.
;   3. "The waitlist migration (survey says 045 - confirm)" -- confirmed exactly.
;      migrations/045_events_waitlist_status.sql:4-9 drops the two-value CHECK and re-adds it with
;      three. That is the whole of the waitlist's storage: no separate table, no position column,
;      no joined_at beyond created_at.
;   4. "What happens at exactly capacity" has TWO answers, not one, and the survey implies one.
;      The last seat is sold (:626, strict `>`), and the same instant opens the waitlist (:1359,
;      strict `<`). Both are pinned below, and the complementarity is an invariant.
;   5. The same-day question has no limit to find. migrations/043 declares no unique key over
;      `events` beyond the primary key at :6, and src/api/events.rs:1454-1477 is a plain INSERT
;      with no ON CONFLICT arm. tests/integration_events_same_day.rs designs four events onto one
;      date through the admin handler (:279-375) -- but all four of its tests are `#[ignore]`d
;      (:134, :210, :237, :278) and return early without a database, so the test is a named case
;      and not a proof, and the schema is what carries the verdict. The real rule
;      the test names at :68-72 is a GROUPING rule, and it is a timezone rule: the date comes from
;      the market-local instant (src/ui/screens/events_screen.rs:73-77 over :63-67), so two events
;      can share a calendar day while their UTC days differ.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24, refutation 1's last sentence: "the events screens are two of them" was
; false when written. The events paths were never members of turbobaby/legacy-retirement's
; LEGACY_LIVE_ROUTES, whose members and count are that file's to state; which is why that set did
; not change when the owner's ruling repointed the three event paths on 2026-09-24.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It carries no attendee: no telegram id, no handle, no first name, no
; booking id, no event fixture standing for a real evening. The guest-list formatter's own
; identifiers are named by path and never by value. It invents no capacity: the tree defines no
; event TYPE at all -- no column in migrations 043, 045, 051, 052, 055 or 070, no variant in
; src/db/entities/event.rs -- so a per-type seat count would be a number this repository has never
; held, and the refusal is declared instead. It quotes no Cyrillic shipped string: the reminder
; body, the guest-list header and the empty-list line are cited by path and line, never by
; wording. It states no price and no currency; a Stars amount appears only as the abstract
; quantity a promotion must clear. It declares no HTTP numeral a sibling already owns. Nothing
; from D14 -- no renter, handle, phone, key code, plate, debt, purchase price or personal note --
; in a constant, a comment or a test.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-events-booking;

