; --- Ownership edges ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The pinned compiler lowers a brace import to an empty UseDecl and the gate rejects it, so a
; cross-contract edge is a string holding the owner's ID plus a test asserting the literal. Every
; edge below is named by ID and by the NAME of the declaration it leans on, never by line.
;
; CORRECTED 2026-09-21. This paragraph used to say "ten contracts were written beside this one in a
; single wave". That number was wrong and wrong in the reassuring direction: counted from git, the
; commit that added this file added THIRTEEN new contracts (and modified a fourteenth), and the TEN
; belongs to the wave BEFORE it. So more siblings were moving under a line number than the sentence
; admitted, not fewer. "Goes stale inside the hour" is dropped with the bad count -- nobody timed
; the interval, and an untimed figure has no place beside measured ones.
;
; The corpus-wide RESIDUE is refused a constant here for a reason that proves the point: counted at
; 63 when this correction began and at 7 a few minutes later, because sibling contracts are being
; repaired in parallel. Pinning a live total would publish a number that goes stale before the
; commit carrying it lands, which is the very defect this paragraph exists to warn about. What is
; pinned is what cannot move: the wave sizes, which are git history, and this file's own
; contribution, which is zero. Citations into src/, migrations/, data/, docs/ and DECISIONS.md are
; different -- those files were not moving -- and they stay.
pub const CORPUS_T27_FILE_COUNT : u8 = 43;
pub const OWN_WAVE_NEW_CONTRACTS : u8 = 13;
pub const PRIOR_WAVE_NEW_CONTRACTS : u8 = 10;
pub const SIBLING_LINE_CITATIONS_IN_THIS_FILE : u8 = 0;
pub const CORPUS_RESIDUE_IS_PINNED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const CORPUS_RESIDUE_NOTE : str = "Counted twice on 2026-09-21 during this correction: 63 at the start and 7 a few minutes later. The drop is sibling contracts being repaired in parallel, not a measurement error. A live corpus-wide total is therefore refused a constant here, because pinning one would publish a number that goes stale before the commit carrying it lands. Any reader who needs today's figure can grep for it in one line; what this file owes is the two wave counts a grep cannot recover, and those are above.";
pub const WAVE_CENSUS_MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
pub const WAVE_CENSUS_SOURCE : str = "git log over specs/turbobaby, added-file counts per commit";
pub const STALENESS_INTERVAL_IS_PUBLISHED : bool = false;

pub fn edge_is_durable(names_a_declaration: bool, names_a_line_number: bool) bool {
  return names_a_declaration and !names_a_line_number;
}
;
; legacy-retirement owns the one distinction this file would otherwise have had to invent: that
; hiding DATA and retiring a SURFACE are different acts. Its HIDDEN_TABLES array already names
; `events` and its data_decision_changes_the_surface already answers no. This file therefore
; declares no retirement state of its own; it declares only the consequence for a NEW row, which
; that contract does not cover because a visibility flag cannot reach a row that does not exist.
pub const REUSES_LEGACY_RETIREMENT_ID : str = "turbobaby/legacy-retirement";
; market owns the shop clock -- the offset, the zone name and the fact that it has no DST, in
; TH_UTC_OFFSET_HOURS, TH_TIMEZONE and TH_DST. This file consumes the offset as an abstract whole
; number of hours east and declares no zone, no offset literal and no DST rule. That discipline is
; not decorative: src/api/events.rs:2063-2067 records a repaired bug where a hardcoded seven-hour
; shift was typed UTC, and the repaired call at :1928 goes through the market clock.
pub const REUSES_MARKET_ID : str = "turbobaby/market";
; locale-policy owns the published locale set and what an unpublished one renders, in
; PUBLISHED_LOCALES and resolution_is_total. Every customer-facing sentence on this surface is a
; key in src/trios/i18n.rs selected at src/api/events.rs:2080-2084 and throughout the events
; screen; this file pins the obligation that a sentence exists and never the sentence.
pub const REUSES_LOCALE_POLICY_ID : str = "turbobaby/locale-policy";
; notification-queue owns a queued outbound message: its row, its attempt budget and its drain, in
; MAX_ATTEMPTS and drain_admits_row. Named here precisely because this surface does NOT use it --
; see refutation 2 in the header. The abstract parameter this file takes from that contract is a
; single boolean, is_queue_row, and the attempt count it implies.
pub const REUSES_NOTIFICATION_QUEUE_ID : str = "turbobaby/notification-queue";
; request-identity owns who a request is and the three gates, in identity_of_request and
; strict_proof_ok. This file takes the gate's verdict as booleans and restates no gate, no
; precedence and no attempt bound. Worth naming for one measured reason: the handle stored on a
; booking row comes from validated initData and never from the request body
; (src/api/events.rs:348-362 says why), so the identity edge is load-bearing on the guest list and
; not only on the door.
pub const REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";
; rate-limit owns whether an attempt is admitted inside a window, in attempt_admitted. This file
; makes two statements about that surface -- book_event carries a limiter (src/api/events.rs:528-540
; with the budget at :25-26) and join_waitlist carries none (:1307-1405) -- and declares neither
; budget, neither window nor any admission rule. The edge is added 2026-09-21 by this file's
; adversarial review so that nobody later writes the event-booking budget into a booking contract.
pub const REUSES_RATE_LIMIT_ID : str = "turbobaby/rate-limit";
; promo-broadcast was not in this file's brief and is owed anyway: it already owns what a SOLD-OUT
; event is worth to the promo sweeper, in the rule its own invariant calls
; a_sold_out_event_is_ranked_below_everything_that_still_has_a_seat. That contract consumes the
; verdict; this one defines it. The seam is one grep away and is named so nobody defines
; "sold out" twice.
pub const REUSES_PROMO_BROADCAST_ID : str = "turbobaby/promo-broadcast";
pub const REUSE_EDGE_COUNT : u8 = 7;

